From 2a4ac3f2e72f8f473ac96ed78c5ae9178cac595e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: leow149 <leow149@lucidmail.xyz>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 16:29:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 105/106] arm64: dts: allwinner: a100: Move the display
 pipeline and PWM to the SoC dtsi

The display engine, its DE2 bus with the mixer, the DPSS TOP, TCON LCD,
MIPI DSI and D-PHY, and the PWM controller are SoC blocks, so describe them
in sun50i-a100.dtsi (DSI, D-PHY and PWM disabled by default) and only
enable them, attach the panel and pick the PWM pin in the TrimUI Smart Pro
DT. The DPSS TOP no longer lists a filler "tcon-tv0" clock: this SoC has
no TCON TV and the binding and driver now say so.

While at it, tidy up the board DT: drop the stale "WiFi/BT/GPU not
described" note, put misplaced comments back on their nodes, move the
Bluetooth rfkill node into the root node and explain why the BL31
reservation lives here (TF-A only adds it to U-Boot's own DT).

No functional change intended.

Signed-off-by: leow149 <leow149@lucidmail.xyz>
---
 .../arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-a100.dtsi | 177 ++++++++++++
 .../allwinner/sun50i-a133-trimui-smartpro.dts | 260 +++---------------
 2 files changed, 222 insertions(+), 215 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-a100.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-a100.dtsi
